cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LOXDockAudit in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software
title: "LOXDockAudit: A Reproducible Framework for Control-Aware Productive Geometry Analysis in LOX-Collagen Docking Screens"
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-05-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/G1F12/LOXDockAudit"
url: "https://github.com/G1F12/LOXDockAudit"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20241797"
abstract: >
  LOXDockAudit is a negative-control-aware computational triage tool
  for LOX-Collagen engineering. It evaluates whether engineered LOX
  constructs are positioned near collagen Lys/Hyl substrate residues
  in potentially productive catalytic geometry. Features include
  active-site-to-substrate distance scoring, control-aware screen
  comparison, structural QC (His triad, Lys-Tyr, disulfide geometry),
  input auditing with SHA256 verification, and reproducible real
  HDOCK dataset validation.
keywords:
  - lysyl oxidase
  - collagen
  - protein engineering
  - docking
  - structural biology
  - bioinformatics
  - reproducibility
